config DEXP_VETO
	bool "DexProtector SIGKILL veto (anti-watchdog)"
	depends on KRETPROBES && KALLSYMS
	default n
	help
	  Built-in driver that vetoes SIGKILL to a configurable app uid via a
	  kretprobe on security_task_kill(), defeating DexProtector's external
	  anti-frida watchdog. Control at runtime through /sys/kernel/dexp_veto/
	  (uid, verbose, hide_uid). Inert until armed (uid defaults to -1).

	  Say Y to compile it in. There is no loadable-module form (avoids the
	  GKI MODVERSIONS/CRC problem). If unsure, say N.
